      "message": "We don\u0027t support using ../ to escape out of the current directory anywhere else, we shouldn\u0027t here either. This helps make it really obvious that others are referring to files in your directory, since you, or a parent, has to export it. We\u0027d prefer not to use absolute paths either, but we haven\u0027t gone that far yet.\n\nIn prebuilts/gcc/linux-x86/host/x86_64-w64-mingw32-4.8/Android.bp, add a filegroup definition:\n\n  filegroup {\n    name: \"winpthreads.COPYING\",\n    srcs: [\"licenses/mingw-w64-svn-r5861/mingw-w64-libraries/winpthreads/COPYING\"],\n  }\n\nThen here you can use:\n\n  notice: \":winpthreads.COPYING\",\n\nYou\u0027ll need to use ctx.ExpandSource / ExtractSourceDeps for it to resolve the filegroup. Then we won\u0027t need to prefix $(LOCAL_PATH)/ in androidmk.go",
